# Checker-verified pages are byte-exact by contract: the scripts in notes/scripts/ regex on
# `*"…"` quotation markers, on `| n |` table cells with no cell padding, and on block-quote line
# positions. Prettier 3.9.9 rewrites all three (measured 2026-10-14 over the 1,096 pages under
# notes/: 630 `*x*` -> `_x_`, 279 `*"…"` -> `_"…"`, and 10,392 table rows not in single-space
# form, which the printer pads) and its markdown printer exposes only proseWrap and singleQuote,
# so none of it is configurable. Format only the two pages no checker parses, listed below.
# notes/scripts/README.md is excluded for the same reason: its checker's needles match unpadded
# table cells and `**N**` counts verbatim, and its mutant set asserts those needles fire.
# upstream_history pages carry the same two byte-forms: `*"…"` quotations pinned to `path:line`
# anchors, and unpadded cells in their change tables. The pages moved under notes/ on 2026-10-10,
# so the rule has to name the new path — notes/*.md is top-level only and does not reach them.
# Measured 2026-10-14: `prettier --check "notes/**/*.md"` reported 28 pages as needing a rewrite
# before this pass — 23 under notes/reports/ and 5 under notes/development/ — because the rule
# named top-level notes/*.md, scripts, summaries and upstream_history and reached none of them.
# Those 28 carry 1,495 table rows, 1,213 of them single-space-padded, and 236 `*"…"` markers, so
# widening the two padding-fragile row regexes to `\s*` would fix the cells on 2 pages and leave
# the markers on 28. 5 of the 28 are render-diffed by verify_page_sync.py, so the two negations
# that un-ignored notes/reports/links.md and notes/reports/proof-density.md named pages a checker
# does parse; they are removed.
notes/*.md
notes/scripts/**/*.md
notes/summaries/**/*.md
notes/development/upstream_history/*.md
notes/reports/*.md
notes/development/*.md
!notes/reports/conjecture-standing.md
!notes/development/summaries-workflow.md

